---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../../shared/config/config";

const siteTitle = "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform";
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle={siteTitle}
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Relapse After 30 Days — Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  description="What community members report about relapsing after about a month without pornography use."
  canonical="/relapse/after-30-days/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "About Relapse", url: "/relapse/" },
    { name: "After 30 days", url: "/relapse/after-30-days/" },
  ]}
>
  <h1>Relapse After 30 Days</h1>
  <p>Some community members describe a relapse after about a month of not using
  pornography. This page reports what they describe, without claiming that any timeline
  applies to you.</p>

  <h2>What members report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A relapse around a month in is often described as following a stressful event or a
    change in routine, rather than a sudden loss of motivation.</li>
    <li>Some members describe relaxing the strategies that got them through the first weeks
    — for example, returning the phone to the bedroom or easing restrictions.</li>
    <li>Many describe the relapse as discouraging precisely because a month felt like a
    meaningful milestone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this means</h2>
  <p>Thirty days is a common milestone in recovery communities, but it is not an
  established threshold with any demonstrated significance. A relapse at this point is not
  more or less meaningful than a relapse at any other time.</p>

  <p class="note">The useful question is not "why did I fail at 30 days" but "what preceded
  this, and what can I change." See <a href="/relapse/recovery-after-relapse/">recovering
  after a relapse</a> and <a href="/problems/why-do-relapses-happen-after-a-long-streak/">why
  relapses happen after a long streak</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
